OL,3,GNEWSASpeed fines cash should fund road
OL,4,Asafety - council
OL,5,
OL,6,FRotherham councillors have backed calls
OL,7,Ffor half the money raised through local
OL,8,Fspeeding fines to be spent on making
OL,9,Froads safer.
OL,11,FThe Liberal Democrat motion, proposed
OL,12,Fby Councillor Drew Tarmey, called for
OL,13,Flocal authorities to receive 50% of
OL,14,Fspeeding fine revenue from their areas,
OL,15,Fwith the funds ring-fenced for road
OL,16,Fsafety improvements.
OL,18,FTarmey noted fines revenue gets paid to
OL,19,Fthe Treasury, saying the plan would
OL,20,Fgive communities "more of a say" over
OL,21,Fhow the money is spent.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
